From 28749e08d3c72d21451bb98eb145ab7b592466c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:08:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(maic): translate the last two player labels, built from a
 ternary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`aria-label={engineState === 'playing' ? 'Pause' : 'Play'}` and the Mute/Unmute
pair beside it were assembled rather than written as literals, so the sweep for
`aria-label="..."` walked past them and the re-test after the first fix still
showed two English tooltips in a Thai classroom. toolbar.play / pause / mute /
unmute added in 13 languages.

Verified on the running container: zero English aria-labels left, zero Chinese,
zero brand. Note for anyone re-testing — Next serves content-hashed chunks and
the browser will happily keep the previous document, so a rebuild needs a
cache-busting reload before the new locale chunk is fetched. Two rounds of
"the fix did nothing" here were that and nothing else.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
